{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Python 3 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Python 3 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nSometimes one has to spell email addresses over the phone. Then one usually pronounces a dot as dot, an at sign as at. As a result, we get something like vasyaatgmaildotcom. Your task is to transform it into a proper email address (vasya@gmail.com). It is known that a proper email address contains only such symbols as . @ and lower-case Latin letters, doesn't start with and doesn't end with a dot. Also, a proper email address doesn't start with and doesn't end with an at sign. Moreover, an email address contains exactly one such symbol as @, yet may contain any number (possible, zero) of dots. You have to carry out a series of replacements so that the length of the result was as short as possible and it was a proper email address. If the lengths are equal, you should print the lexicographically minimal result. Overall, two variants of replacement are possible: dot can be replaced by a dot, at can be replaced by an at. \n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Python 3 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_3>\nn = input()\n\n# Replace first 'at' after position 0\nparts = n.split('at', 1)\nif len(parts) > 1 and n.find('at', 1) != -1:\n    idx = n.find('at', 1)\n    n = n[:idx] + '@' + n[idx+2:]\n\n# Replace all 'dot' after position 0\nwhile True:\n    idx = n.find('dot', 1)\n    if idx == -1 or idx > len(n) - 3:\n        break\n    n = n[:idx] + '.' + n[idx+3:]\n\nprint(n)\n</your_rewritten_code_3>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\ns = input()\n\n# Find the position of '@' - must exist and not at start or end\nat_pos = s.find('at')\nif at_pos == -1:\n    # No 'at' found, invalid input but we'll try to handle\n    print(s)\nelse:\n    # Replace first occurrence of 'at' (not at start) with '@'\n    # We need to find 'at' that's not at position 0 or len-2\n    at_idx = -1\n    for i in range(1, len(s) - 2):\n        if s[i:i+2] == 'at':\n            at_idx = i\n            break\n    \n    if at_idx == -1:\n        # Try to find any 'at' that's not at boundaries\n        for i in range(1, len(s) - 2):\n            if s[i:i+2] == 'at':\n                at_idx = i\n                break\n    \n    if at_idx == -1:\n        print(s)\n    else:\n        # Split into parts\n        before_at = s[:at_idx]\n        after_at = s[at_idx+2:]\n        \n        # Process the part before '@' - replace 'dot' with '.'\n        result_before = before_at\n        i = 1  # Start from position 1 to avoid leading dot\n        while i < len(result_before) - 2:\n            if result_before[i:i+3] == 'dot':\n                result_before = result_before[:i] + '.' + result_before[i+3:]\n            else:\n                i += 1\n        \n        # Process the part after '@' - replace 'dot' with '.'\n        result_after = after_at\n        i = 0\n        while i < len(result_after) - 2:\n            if result_after[i:i+3] == 'dot':\n                result_after = result_after[:i] + '.' + result_after[i+3:]\n            else:\n                i += 1\n        \n        # Ensure no leading/trailing dots or @\n        # Remove leading/trailing dots from before_at part\n        result_before = result_before.lstrip('.')\n        result_before = result_before.rstrip('.')\n        \n        # Remove leading/trailing dots from after_at part\n        result_after = result_after.lstrip('.')\n        result_after = result_after.rstrip('.')\n        \n        # Build final email\n        email = result_before + '@' + result_after\n        \n        # Final validation - ensure no consecutive dots, no leading/trailing dots or @\n        # Remove consecutive dots\n        while '..' in email:\n            email = email.replace('..', '.')\n        \n        # Ensure doesn't start or end with dot or @\n        email = email.strip('.')\n        email = email.strip('@')\n        \n        print(email)\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.3\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0008282806375063956, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.6365746855735779, -3.814689989667386e-06, -5.602820692729438e-06, -0.28262031078338623, -9.417489309271332e-06, -0.6749637126922607, -0.028555061668157578, -0.09234084188938141, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.5772176384925842, -0.0003493413969408721, -0.984649658203125, -0.4728623032569885, -0.09663806855678558, -0.005775312427431345, -0.07798752188682556, -0.25203022360801697, -0.06164979934692383, -0.6328234672546387, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -0.00026544384309090674, -0.25409451127052307, -0.00807236973196268, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.020581724122166634, -3.933898824470816e-06, -0.020553579553961754, -5.8053239627042785e-05, -0.0006123098428361118, -0.31684914231300354, -4.6491513785440475e-06, -2.145764938177308e-06, -0.034479137510061264, -0.0003800861886702478, 0.0, -0.06993867456912994, -2.264974000354414e-06, -0.14285998046398163, -0.7145190834999084, -0.023846369236707687, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.001193168922327